PARTITION

Creates an equal-sized GPT layout on an additional data drive. Existing layouts are preserved unless replacement is explicitly confirmed.

Usage:
    partition <drive-number> <count>
    partition <drive-number> <count> --replace --yes

Drive numbers are zero-based, matching DRIVES (Drive0 is entered as 0).
The count is how many partitions to create, from 1 to 16. Newly created partitions are addressed by FORMAT as indexes 0 through count-1.

Example:
    partition 0 2
    format 0 0 fat32 --yes
    format 0 1 fat32 --yes

The --replace form destroys the existing partition table and data.
